{"step_index":161,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T18:21:09Z","thinking":"**Clarifying DNC Requirements**\n\nI've been reviewing the DNC protocol and have an important clarification. Even if someone's on the DNC list, accepting a call request via a form is permissible until they actively opt out of calls. The DNC functionality should definitely be in the app, but it should not automatically block these user-initiated requests. This means that my earlier understanding was not quite right, and the solution can be more permissive.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\types\\index.ts","toolAction":"Viewing types index.ts","toolSummary":"View index.ts"}}]}
