ing a call is allowed until they request to not be called.  that DNC button should be in the app, but it should not try to connect to and read the registry.\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n- **DNC Simplification & Registry Decoupling:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"you can ease up on the DNC stuff. even if someone is on the list, filling out a form and requesting a call is allowed until they request to not be called. that DNC button should be in the app, but it should not try to connect to and read the registry.\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (partially completed in `src/types/index.ts`, `src/db/settingsRepository.ts`, `src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx`; `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx` and `src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx` need final cleanup of any leftover DNC registry checks or suppression filtering).\n- **Physical Device / Live Testing on iPhone:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"how can i get this tested on my phone\"` & `\"considering all the connection issues, we might as well build up all that we can and worry about connecting to test later.\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION / DEFERRED FOR TESTING** (Cloudflare tunnel `npx localtunnel --port 8081` or standalone EAS build planned for rapid testing).\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n- **Telephony & DNC Rules:**\n  - Quote: `\"even if someone is on the list, filling out a form and requesting a call is allowed until they request to not be called. that DNC button should be in the app, but it should not try to connect to and read the registry.\"`\n  - *Meaning:* Do NOT block/filter incoming leads against any global DNC list or external registry. The DNC button in the HUD and Lead Detail screen is simply a 1-tap outcome/disposition button that tags that specific lead as `do_not_call` so the dialer does not recycle them in subsequent retries.\n- **Cost & Backend Preference:**\n  - Backend must be \\$0 recurring hosting cost $\\rightarrow$ SQLite on-device local persistence.\n  - Nat